WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.005
[Ki-jun groans]
Where are we going?

00:47.088 --> 00:49.966
- [Ha-kyung] Shut up and come on.
- [Ki-jun] Why were all those people there?

00:50.049 --> 00:52.343
I saw that bastard Lee Si…
[groans]

00:53.094 --> 00:54.512
You're in no place to ask questions.

00:54.596 --> 00:56.681
You burst into my home
in the middle of the night causing drama.

00:56.765 --> 00:57.891
Why? Tell me why!

00:58.850 --> 01:00.894
Uh, Ha-kyung…

01:01.478 --> 01:03.063
You're being scary.

01:03.146 --> 01:06.316
You think? You showed up drunk
on my doorstep and you're scared of me?

01:07.317 --> 01:08.943
[exhales sharply]

01:09.027 --> 01:11.029
Yeah, you should be happy.

01:11.112 --> 01:14.157
I'm here, 'cause I wanted
to apologize to you.

01:14.783 --> 01:16.284
What?

01:17.786 --> 01:19.913
It's all my fault, Ha-kyung.

01:23.833 --> 01:24.834
Sorry.

01:25.543 --> 01:26.753
I'm so sorry.

01:27.378 --> 01:30.507
I really need you to know that.

01:30.590 --> 01:32.717
[quirky music]

01:32.801 --> 01:35.887
I'm a real asshole. I know it.

01:41.100 --> 01:43.144
They called off their wedding,
isn't that right?

01:44.062 --> 01:45.063
Yeah.

01:46.272 --> 01:47.649
Why did he come here, then?

01:48.358 --> 01:49.275
Don't know.

01:52.320 --> 01:53.988
He was drunk, I think.

01:54.072 --> 01:55.573
I could check if they're okay.

01:57.534 --> 01:58.785
I'd leave them alone.

02:01.746 --> 02:03.081
I'm gonna go find them.

02:03.164 --> 02:05.333
[quirky music continues]

02:06.501 --> 02:07.502
[door opens]

02:08.795 --> 02:09.838
[door closes]

02:09.921 --> 02:11.214
I'm going home.

02:12.423 --> 02:13.591
Seok-ho.

02:15.927 --> 02:17.679
Your apartment's right upstairs?

02:17.762 --> 02:19.055
Yes. Why?

02:19.139 --> 02:20.223
Mm.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.852
Well, actually…

02:25.562 --> 02:28.731
It feels weird sleeping here.
So maybe I could--

02:28.815 --> 02:31.317
- That's not weird. You'll get used to it.
- You think? That's good.

02:31.401 --> 02:33.194
- Oh, yeah. See you at work.
- Mm.

02:33.278 --> 02:34.571
Okay. Bye.

02:37.198 --> 02:39.075
You just shoved me down so fast.

02:39.159 --> 02:41.119
- [door opens]
- [deep inhale]

02:41.202 --> 02:42.120
[door closes]

02:42.203 --> 02:43.830
[door lock beeps]

02:48.084 --> 02:50.295
Are you hurting? Was it painful?

02:52.463 --> 02:54.090
What are you saying?

02:54.173 --> 02:56.885
[breathes deeply]

03:01.431 --> 03:04.392
When you saw that I betrayed you,

03:05.351 --> 03:06.728
did it feel like someone

03:06.811 --> 03:10.773
took your heart, threw it on the ground
and stomped on it a million times?

03:11.566 --> 03:12.400
Oh, no.

03:12.483 --> 03:14.319
It wasn't pain.

03:14.402 --> 03:17.530
Humiliation, that was the bigger thing
I had to get through.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.701
So if you could stop finding ways
to embarrass me, that'd be great, huh?

03:22.911 --> 03:25.246
[whining]

03:25.330 --> 03:27.248
- I understand.
- [groans]

03:28.625 --> 03:31.711
- My love Ha-kyung was embarrassed…
- [quirky music]

03:32.462 --> 03:35.632
[cries]
That's how I ruined your life.

03:37.467 --> 03:39.135
Hey. Come on.

03:39.677 --> 03:42.055
What the hell is wrong with you today?

03:42.639 --> 03:43.723
Ha-kyung.

03:44.766 --> 03:47.310
I think something's punishing me.

03:47.393 --> 03:48.353
What?

03:49.479 --> 03:52.941
I'm being punished,
because I hurt and betrayed you.

03:53.024 --> 03:56.527
[Ki-jun crying]

03:58.321 --> 04:00.198
Hey, it's in the past.

04:00.281 --> 04:02.492
And your tantrum
won't make me proofread your article.

04:03.201 --> 04:05.745
Lee Si-woo, it's all his fault.

04:06.913 --> 04:08.998
He did it to Yu-jin, you know?

04:09.832 --> 04:13.127
He lived with her,
she didn't even know me, but still…

04:14.087 --> 04:16.422
What am I supposed to do now, Ha-kyung?

04:17.674 --> 04:20.468
I sacrificed a lot for the wedding.

04:20.551 --> 04:21.886
[deep inhale]

04:22.637 --> 04:28.685
I hurt you so much, and I didn't mean to
and became the biggest jerk ever.

04:30.019 --> 04:32.605
I just happened to be the biggest jerk.

04:33.481 --> 04:39.320
How could she go and lie to me like that?
She didn't even wanna tell the truth.

04:41.322 --> 04:42.865
She didn't really lie.

04:44.075 --> 04:46.244
But she sure did a good job
of not telling you.

04:47.120 --> 04:49.497
At the end of the day, though,
you're married.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.249
Wouldn't she be upset if she saw

04:51.332 --> 04:53.960
how you're acting
over something she did so long ago?

04:55.712 --> 04:59.507
If you love someone,
you have to accept all of them.

04:59.590 --> 05:01.092
Good and bad, and move on.

05:03.803 --> 05:04.971
Understand, Ki-jun?

05:06.389 --> 05:08.683
- [snoring]
- You're sleeping?

05:09.517 --> 05:10.518
Hey.

05:10.601 --> 05:11.936
[groans]

05:12.520 --> 05:13.354
Hey!

05:14.480 --> 05:15.815
What the hell? Wake up!

05:15.898 --> 05:19.527
This isn't okay!
[groaning]

05:20.987 --> 05:22.488
Oh, God.

05:24.449 --> 05:25.616
Lee Si-woo.

05:25.700 --> 05:27.493
You don't know where he lives, do you?

05:29.620 --> 05:30.997
I don't. I have no idea.

05:40.882 --> 05:43.509
[burbling]

05:47.096 --> 05:48.347
[slurps]

05:49.223 --> 05:50.850
[sighs]
Mmm.

05:52.018 --> 05:53.895
[cell phone buzzing]

05:56.606 --> 06:02.361
LEE SI-WOO

06:08.451 --> 06:09.577
Hello?

06:10.161 --> 06:11.621
Why are you calling so late?

06:12.580 --> 06:14.749
[pensive music]

06:19.045 --> 06:20.880
[tires screech]

06:26.302 --> 06:28.429
[pensive music continues]

06:30.598 --> 06:31.557
Oppa?

06:33.059 --> 06:34.519
I'm sorry.

06:35.353 --> 06:36.854
[Ki-jun] I'm so sorry.

06:37.897 --> 06:39.065
How did this…

06:41.234 --> 06:42.902
How did you… Why are you driving him home?

06:43.694 --> 06:45.571
Your husband can answer better than I can.

06:47.406 --> 06:48.741
- Gosh.
- Here.

06:50.118 --> 06:51.369
[groans]

06:55.206 --> 06:58.209
[Ki-jun moaning]

06:58.292 --> 06:59.418
Okay. I got him.

07:00.419 --> 07:02.505
What were you thinking? You're so drunk.

07:03.506 --> 07:04.423
Ki-jun.

07:05.174 --> 07:07.218
We're going home. Okay?

07:08.761 --> 07:10.179
Wake up and walk.

07:12.056 --> 07:14.517
[Yu-jin groaning]

07:14.600 --> 07:16.769
Why did you go get drunk?

07:18.563 --> 07:19.814
I'm sorry.

07:20.773 --> 07:21.858
I'm sorry.

07:22.358 --> 07:23.734
I bet you are sorry.

07:25.194 --> 07:27.405
I'm so sorry.

07:27.989 --> 07:29.365
Ha-kyung.

07:29.449 --> 07:31.492
[somber music]

07:32.326 --> 07:33.661
My fault.

07:34.912 --> 07:37.790
So, so sorry, Jin Ha-kyung.

07:42.253 --> 07:44.255
[somber music continues]

07:46.966 --> 07:47.884
[scoffs]

07:58.269 --> 07:59.395
[music stops]

08:03.316 --> 08:04.358
[clears throat]

08:07.236 --> 08:08.779
[breathes heavily]

08:19.832 --> 08:20.833
[hisses]

08:22.710 --> 08:23.836
[slurps]

08:29.467 --> 08:32.470
[Si-woo] Bad weather isn't
as obvious as cloudy skies,

08:32.553 --> 08:37.141
unexpected snow and rain,
strong wind, and typhoons.

08:37.225 --> 08:38.684
It can be more subtle.

08:38.768 --> 08:41.521
[somber music]

08:45.483 --> 08:46.817
Why are you still out here?

08:48.611 --> 08:50.196
So you got him back home all right?

08:51.572 --> 08:54.033
I'm sorry, you shouldn't have to do that.

08:54.825 --> 08:55.993
Let's go in.

08:56.077 --> 08:57.870
Does it bother you that much too?

08:58.454 --> 08:59.413
Does what?

09:00.456 --> 09:04.001
That Yu-jin and I were living together?

09:04.085 --> 09:06.671
[Si-woo] Even just
hot weather and humidity

09:06.754 --> 09:08.923
hold people down and affect their moods.

09:09.006 --> 09:10.883
I heard Han Ki-jun talk about it.

09:11.467 --> 09:12.927
Does it bother you like that too?

09:13.636 --> 09:15.972
[dramatic music]

09:17.348 --> 09:18.432
Well…

09:19.141 --> 09:20.977
I wouldn't say I feel like Han Ki-jun.

09:22.186 --> 09:24.313
But it did sting a little bit.

09:25.439 --> 09:28.442
Like when I found out
about you writing all

09:28.526 --> 09:30.820
of Han Ki-jun's columns for him,
and that you still do?

09:30.903 --> 09:32.405
[Si-woo] Heat and humidity…

09:32.488 --> 09:33.447
Is it like that?

09:33.531 --> 09:35.366
…does it put people
more on edge than usual?

09:35.449 --> 09:36.784
Who told you that?

09:39.120 --> 09:40.580
I heard it at work.

09:40.663 --> 09:43.541
- Why didn't you mention it?
- You didn't mention it, either, so…

09:43.624 --> 09:46.502
[Si-woo] People become combative in heat.

09:46.586 --> 09:48.546
It almost seems like
you want to fight with me.

09:48.629 --> 09:50.631
You can at least try to justify it.

09:51.465 --> 09:53.884
[Si-woo] Just like that,
we've been transformed,

09:53.968 --> 09:58.389
irritable and unaware
that it's the weather's doing.

10:00.975 --> 10:03.811
[lock beeping, chimes]

10:03.894 --> 10:06.689
[stomping]

10:06.772 --> 10:07.940
[Dong-han clears throat]

10:10.276 --> 10:11.360
[slams]

10:16.032 --> 10:17.116
[clears throat]

10:22.246 --> 10:23.331
[rustles]

10:25.916 --> 10:28.586
[lock beeping, chimes]

10:29.503 --> 10:30.630
[door slams]

10:30.713 --> 10:31.881
Oh…

10:33.466 --> 10:34.550
[slams]

10:42.600 --> 10:44.894
God, it's so hot.

10:45.478 --> 10:52.443
EPISODE 8
DISCOMFORT INDEX

10:53.319 --> 10:56.155
[soft music]

11:04.872 --> 11:07.541
[soft music continues]

11:15.841 --> 11:17.843
[calm music]

11:29.313 --> 11:31.315
[quirky music]

11:45.663 --> 11:47.081
What happened last night?

11:47.164 --> 11:48.290
[slurps]

11:50.042 --> 11:51.127
What do you mean?

11:52.002 --> 11:53.754
You were totally wasted,

11:53.838 --> 11:56.841
and for some reason,
Lee Si-woo had to bring you home.

11:56.924 --> 11:59.593
- What was that?
- Let's talk later.

11:59.677 --> 12:02.555
I need to know what happened.
You have to tell me right now.

12:05.641 --> 12:07.643
There's no time right now, Yu-jin.

12:09.228 --> 12:12.064
What's wrong? Was it something I did?

12:15.025 --> 12:16.735
I just…
[sighs]

12:17.486 --> 12:19.405
…need some space to think this through.

12:20.030 --> 12:21.157
I'm going to work.

12:24.785 --> 12:25.786
[door opens]

12:26.745 --> 12:28.164
- [gasps]
- [door closes]

12:29.081 --> 12:30.499
[groans]

12:33.252 --> 12:34.253
Wait…

12:36.172 --> 12:39.258
You took… I was going
to clean it this morning.

12:39.341 --> 12:42.386
Let's make a rule that
the food gets cleaned up after eating.

12:42.470 --> 12:44.513
If we don't, the apartment
will absorb the smell.

12:44.597 --> 12:46.724
Of course. I will in the future.

12:48.350 --> 12:49.268
[groans]

12:49.351 --> 12:50.728
Hey, how did you…

12:51.312 --> 12:53.772
You can find ready-made food
on the top left.

12:53.856 --> 12:55.232
Plates and things are on the right.

12:55.316 --> 12:59.028
Perishables like bread and milk
are obviously in the fridge.

12:59.111 --> 13:00.279
So please help yourselves.

13:00.362 --> 13:01.739
I'll see you both at work.

13:03.532 --> 13:04.992
Please, have breakfast.

13:05.075 --> 13:06.285
[Dong-han] Okay. See you.

13:07.077 --> 13:09.038
We'll be there soon.

13:09.121 --> 13:11.123
[cheeky music]

13:12.875 --> 13:13.751
[door opens]

13:15.002 --> 13:15.920
[door slams]

13:16.003 --> 13:17.630
- [door lock beeps]
- Do you want ramen?

13:17.713 --> 13:19.173
- Huh?
- She said have some.

13:20.049 --> 13:22.176
Oh, the ramen is over here.

13:23.886 --> 13:24.887
Over here.

13:24.970 --> 13:27.181
And the pot…

13:27.932 --> 13:31.268
- is here.
- Huh?

13:32.269 --> 13:34.021
How did you know that?

13:34.813 --> 13:35.940
Oh.

13:36.023 --> 13:38.484
I just listened.
She just pointed everything out.

13:39.068 --> 13:40.569
- Oh.
- Yeah.

13:42.196 --> 13:44.532
I'll boil water for us. Okay.

13:45.616 --> 13:46.784
[thuds]

13:46.867 --> 13:50.162
- [tap water running]
- Oh, it's only morning, and it's so hot.

13:50.246 --> 13:52.039
- I'm gonna go shower.
- Okay.

13:53.707 --> 13:55.709
[playful music]

13:58.796 --> 14:03.300
[reporter] This afternoon, we're expecting
the temperature to rise to 30° in Seoul.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.635
Humidity will stay high.

14:04.718 --> 14:07.972
The current discomfort index
in Seoul is 76.7.

14:08.055 --> 14:09.682
So everyone should keep an eye out,

14:09.765 --> 14:12.518
for those feeling moody
from the humidity and heat.

14:13.102 --> 14:15.854
Even though the temperature is almost
the same as the last few days,

14:15.938 --> 14:18.399
the higher humidity
will affect our perception,

14:18.482 --> 14:20.568
so the heat today will feel
even more stifling.

14:20.651 --> 14:24.071
Highest today will be 31 degree in Seoul,
30 in Cheongju.

14:24.154 --> 14:27.157
Like when I found out
about you writing all

14:27.241 --> 14:29.577
of Han Ki-jun's columns for him,
and that you still do?

14:30.160 --> 14:31.620
[Si-woo] Is it like that?

14:36.542 --> 14:42.965
[beeping]

14:45.926 --> 14:47.177
What the…

14:47.261 --> 14:49.013
[beeping]

14:50.764 --> 14:51.891
[yelps]

14:51.974 --> 14:53.017
[brakes squeal]

14:53.100 --> 14:54.143
[gasps]

14:54.226 --> 14:56.478
- [car horns honking]
- [gasps]

14:56.562 --> 14:57.688
[sighs]

14:59.189 --> 15:01.734
[dramatic music]

15:07.448 --> 15:08.449
Miss Kim.

15:08.949 --> 15:10.534
- This is the data.
- [team leader] Morning.

15:10.618 --> 15:12.828
- Hi.
- Good morning.

15:13.621 --> 15:15.247
Good morning.

15:18.667 --> 15:20.669
[background chatter]

15:23.130 --> 15:24.590
[exhales deeply]

15:27.051 --> 15:28.761
[whooshing]

15:32.306 --> 15:34.516
[pensive music]

15:35.768 --> 15:36.852
Oh, thank you.

15:37.436 --> 15:39.188
Hey, it's hot in here, right?

15:39.939 --> 15:42.483
Is it? I don't think so.

15:43.233 --> 15:46.236
You spent too much time with the data
saying you would feel warmer today.

15:46.320 --> 15:47.363
[chuckles]

15:47.988 --> 15:51.492
Or you might be nervous,
because we'll have monsoon soon.

15:51.575 --> 15:52.576
Seriously?

15:53.369 --> 15:54.578
It's getting warm in here.

15:55.204 --> 15:56.121
I told you.

16:01.377 --> 16:02.753
I'm gonna call someone.

16:05.005 --> 16:06.423
[line rings]

16:06.507 --> 16:08.884
Hello, this is the Chief Team
of the Forecast Bureau.

16:08.968 --> 16:10.928
It seems like there's an issue
with our AC unit.

16:11.595 --> 16:13.305
Oh, for real?

16:13.931 --> 16:14.974
[sighs]

16:15.057 --> 16:16.433
We're starting the meeting soon.

16:17.476 --> 16:19.853
Okay. Please do it as soon as possible.

16:22.314 --> 16:24.316
- Hey.
- [employee 1] Hello, sir.

16:25.859 --> 16:27.528
Are we not running the AC?

16:27.611 --> 16:29.613
There's a problem
with the AC in the whole building,

16:29.697 --> 16:32.449
but, um, they dispatched
the Repair Team to fix it.

16:32.533 --> 16:35.327
Oh, not today, of all days.

16:35.411 --> 16:36.328
Okay.

16:37.329 --> 16:39.039
Shouldn't Director Jin be here?

16:40.541 --> 16:41.583
I don't know.

16:42.459 --> 16:44.670
- She left before we did, so…
- [cell phone buzzing]

16:44.753 --> 16:45.713
[Dong-han] Yeah.

16:47.840 --> 16:48.924
[door slides open]

16:54.513 --> 16:55.931
Hey, Ha-kyung. What do you need?

16:56.015 --> 16:58.225
My car insurance
is Areumhaesang, isn't it?

16:58.308 --> 16:59.727
I changed it.

16:59.810 --> 17:01.979
I moved it over to the company
that Sang-hun works for.

17:02.062 --> 17:03.772
What? And you didn't let me know?

17:03.856 --> 17:06.358
[tense music]

17:08.736 --> 17:09.695
Hey.

17:09.778 --> 17:11.447
You're calling your insurance or what?

17:11.530 --> 17:13.365
What do you think I'm doing right now?

17:14.408 --> 17:16.076
Okay. What's this company called?

17:16.660 --> 17:18.954
- Oh, come on. I don't have all day--
- Yes, I'm aware!

17:20.914 --> 17:22.499
So where are you? I'll take my car.

17:22.583 --> 17:23.500
No, don't.

17:23.584 --> 17:25.753
Just give me the name for the company.

17:25.836 --> 17:29.006
I'll handle it for you.
I'm coming now to meet up with you.

17:30.090 --> 17:33.177
[female voice] The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

17:33.260 --> 17:34.303
Please try again.

17:34.386 --> 17:36.472
[tense music continues]

17:38.098 --> 17:38.974
Okay.

17:39.641 --> 17:42.811
Do what you have to do. All right. Mm-hm.

17:43.771 --> 17:45.105
- Sir.
- Hm?

17:45.189 --> 17:47.775
Director Jin got in a car accident
on her way here.

17:47.858 --> 17:49.234
- [woman gasps]
- [Bong-chan] What?

17:49.318 --> 17:50.569
[groans]

17:51.487 --> 17:52.613
Well, is she okay?

17:52.696 --> 17:54.490
Yeah, she's all right.
[inhales]

17:54.573 --> 17:56.450
Anyway, I can sit in for her. Okay?

17:56.533 --> 17:57.534
[Bong-chan] Okay.

17:59.912 --> 18:03.582
On today of all days
when we've got an important briefing.

18:03.665 --> 18:08.087
[groans]
Is this a bad sign for the season?

18:08.170 --> 18:09.838
[gasps]
Don't jinx it.

18:10.631 --> 18:12.925
It's just the weather
putting everyone on edge.

18:13.467 --> 18:15.302
Don't read into it too much, Miss Kim.

18:15.385 --> 18:16.303
Okay.

18:23.560 --> 18:25.604
Hey, uh, shouldn't Mr. Han be here?

18:25.687 --> 18:29.358
Uh, he said something came up.
He told me to fill in for him today.

18:35.405 --> 18:37.574
[dramatic music]

18:39.076 --> 18:41.495
Let's commence
the forecast discussion for June 27.

18:41.578 --> 18:42.871
Satellite Center, you there?

18:43.455 --> 18:46.416
Yes, if you look at the satellite image
and this chart,

18:46.500 --> 18:50.212
there's a stationary front of waves out
over the sea by the Southern Jeju.

18:51.004 --> 18:52.589
[Si-woo] I heard you got in an accident.

18:53.173 --> 18:54.758
Please call me when you can.

18:56.218 --> 18:58.720
[revving]

18:59.930 --> 19:03.142
Since no one got hurt,
insurance should cover it all. Easy.

19:03.225 --> 19:05.102
- Thank you, sir.
- Just sign right here.

19:05.185 --> 19:06.103
Okay.

19:10.023 --> 19:12.025
All right. I'll call you later
about the car.

19:15.070 --> 19:16.905
[truck engine starts]

19:17.823 --> 19:18.907
[sighs]

19:18.991 --> 19:21.118
[dramatic music]

19:25.873 --> 19:27.875
[engine revs]

19:29.251 --> 19:30.919
[engine revs]

19:40.762 --> 19:42.222
[whooshes]

19:43.098 --> 19:45.225
What are you doing here?
I said not to come.

19:45.309 --> 19:47.227
I was on the phone with Sang-hun
on my way over,

19:47.311 --> 19:50.355
and he said he'll do
the necessary paperwork and everything,

19:50.439 --> 19:51.565
and call you later.

19:51.648 --> 19:54.193
Why did you change
my insurance without telling me?

19:54.276 --> 19:56.403
It's made this whole thing way harder.

19:56.486 --> 19:57.654
My bad.
[sighs]

19:57.738 --> 20:00.199
It's 'cause I thought we'd only have
one car after we got married.

20:00.282 --> 20:02.701
Mine expired,
and I wanted to help my friend.

20:03.202 --> 20:05.078
If I knew where we were headed,
I wouldn't have--

20:05.162 --> 20:07.372
You always do this, you know?
You're impulsive.

20:07.456 --> 20:09.917
You do whatever you want,
and then I have to clean it up.

20:10.000 --> 20:11.376
Well, I fixed this.

20:11.460 --> 20:13.503
Well, then good for you. You can go now.

20:13.587 --> 20:15.881
All right. Hop in now. We're already late.

20:16.632 --> 20:17.466
I'm okay.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.802
I told Mr. Um to handle all of that.

20:20.886 --> 20:22.304
I am late, but I'll get a taxi.

20:22.387 --> 20:23.388
- So I should--
- Huh?

20:23.889 --> 20:26.391
You think a taxi will pick you up
from down here?

20:26.475 --> 20:27.434
[scoffs]

20:27.517 --> 20:29.978
[vehicle horn honking]

20:30.687 --> 20:33.065
I HEARD YOU GOT IN AN ACCIDENT.
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU CAN.

20:34.358 --> 20:38.445
[Bong-chan] In conclusion, we expect
the stationary front will cause rainfall

20:38.528 --> 20:41.281
in Southern Jeju, in five days from now.

20:41.365 --> 20:45.494
Ah, we'll keep an eye on the atmosphere
over the ocean. You just never know.

20:45.577 --> 20:48.664
'Cause if the front keeps going north
and then goes south,

20:48.747 --> 20:50.374
there's a chance the rain start later.

20:50.457 --> 20:53.585
The North Pacific anticyclone
is pulling in the Southeast.

20:53.669 --> 20:55.462
Otherwise, we would've
taken that into account.

20:55.545 --> 20:59.007
However, it's possible the rain
may come early, it just couldn't be later.

20:59.091 --> 21:00.759
If you look at Jeju Sea,

21:00.842 --> 21:02.928
the atmosphere looks like
it's hardly moving at all.

21:03.595 --> 21:06.765
[Dong-han] If that trough doesn't maintain
its current altitude of five kilometers

21:06.848 --> 21:09.601
- or the North Pacific anticyclone…
- [Si-woo] What happened?

21:09.685 --> 21:10.936
Hey. Are you okay?

21:11.019 --> 21:12.646
[Dong-han] The front could shift.

21:12.729 --> 21:15.399
It could remain north-headed
and then fall back to the south.

21:15.482 --> 21:17.776
If the pressure system contributes,
and it maintains

21:17.859 --> 21:20.612
the five-kilometer altitude,
then it would be worth following.

21:21.488 --> 21:23.490
Jeju Office, let's hear from you.

21:23.573 --> 21:25.826
[employee 2] I agree
with the Busan Office.

21:25.909 --> 21:28.996
With that gale, 200hPAs
above the north side

21:29.079 --> 21:33.083
 of the stationary front,
it's likely the rain will develop sooner.

21:33.166 --> 21:35.335
[pensive music]

21:35.419 --> 21:36.586
Hm…

21:38.964 --> 21:41.591
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

21:49.433 --> 21:51.643
[pensive music continues]

21:59.776 --> 22:01.528
[employee 3]
Think about the public response.

22:01.611 --> 22:05.157
Imagine the criticism if it rains earlier,
and the public isn't prepared.

22:05.240 --> 22:07.576
[employee 2] With rain,
even when we're just a day late,

22:07.659 --> 22:09.953
the criticism is worse
than being days early.

22:10.746 --> 22:12.039
It's better to play it safe.

22:12.706 --> 22:15.000
Not when the data is this clear.

22:16.001 --> 22:18.628
We've seen our weather
get more and more fickle,

22:18.712 --> 22:20.088
because of climate change.

22:21.381 --> 22:22.883
Almost every year for several seasons,

22:22.966 --> 22:24.843
we missed the mark on the end
of monsoon season,

22:24.926 --> 22:26.678
even though we really tried.

22:26.762 --> 22:29.181
Almost no one trusts
the forecast any longer.

22:29.765 --> 22:33.060
So, if we get the first day
of the season wrong too,

22:34.061 --> 22:36.980
I can't even imagine the amount
of criticism we'd get from that.

22:37.064 --> 22:38.940
Do you think it's worth the risk?

22:39.024 --> 22:40.901
[pensive music]

22:42.277 --> 22:46.114
Well, then we could postpone
the announcement if we had to.

22:47.949 --> 22:50.786
- What's the rule? Can we do that?
- We've already postponed it quite a bit.

22:50.869 --> 22:53.330
Presses and local officials
are already calling

22:53.413 --> 22:55.540
that they were alerted
to the current conditions.

22:55.624 --> 22:57.459
So they really wanna know our thoughts.

22:57.542 --> 23:00.545
If we did, they'll have another excuse
to publish whatever.

23:00.629 --> 23:03.507
Don't you remember
how awful it went last time?

23:03.590 --> 23:05.008
[inhales]
Mr. Lee, thoughts?

23:06.802 --> 23:08.428
[breathes heavily]

23:13.517 --> 23:14.559
Lee Si-woo.

23:15.936 --> 23:16.978
What do you think?

23:27.614 --> 23:28.448
I apologize.

23:29.241 --> 23:30.867
I missed a little of what you were saying.

23:30.951 --> 23:32.244
You kidding?

23:33.411 --> 23:34.663
[Si-woo] I'm sorry.

23:35.622 --> 23:36.581
[sighs]

23:37.541 --> 23:39.209
Okay. What's the plan?

23:39.709 --> 23:42.045
[Bong-chan] Due to the trough
in northern central China,

23:42.129 --> 23:43.922
and the formation of the gale,

23:44.005 --> 23:46.216
there's a higher probability
that the stationary front

23:46.299 --> 23:47.676
will travel to the north, right?

23:48.385 --> 23:51.513
Do we expect rainfall
in the next five days or don't we?

23:52.889 --> 23:55.475
We have to. Yeah. Announce it, it's fine.

23:57.018 --> 23:58.770
- [Bong-chan] You're sure?
- Yes, sir.

24:02.899 --> 24:04.901
Okay. Well, get to it.

24:04.985 --> 24:05.986
[Bong-chan groans]

24:06.069 --> 24:09.197
Let's also prepare
for a press briefing this afternoon.

24:09.281 --> 24:11.199
Oh, also, at the briefing today,

24:11.283 --> 24:12.951
the Office of Spokesperson
should emphasize

24:13.034 --> 24:15.120
that the journalists should not
jump to conclusions

24:15.203 --> 24:17.080
or overstate any dates at all.

24:17.164 --> 24:18.999
- unlike what they did last year.
- Yes.

24:19.082 --> 24:21.042
Hm? Well done, everyone.

24:21.126 --> 24:23.795
- Thank you all.
- [employees] Thank you.

24:28.592 --> 24:30.427
[footsteps receding]

24:35.473 --> 24:37.726
[engine revving]

24:39.477 --> 24:41.646
[engine rumbling]

24:43.732 --> 24:46.610
- Who's covering you?
- Oh, Assistant Director Kim said he could.

24:47.402 --> 24:48.695
Well, that's fantastic.

24:53.116 --> 24:54.117
Sorry for yesterday.

24:55.076 --> 24:56.620
I drank way too much.

24:57.162 --> 24:58.747
Was it really bad?

24:59.331 --> 25:00.207
[scoffs]

25:00.749 --> 25:02.584
You already know, so why are you asking?

25:04.211 --> 25:05.962
I'm sorry.
[sighs]

25:07.172 --> 25:09.382
- You have to get over.
- Hm?

25:10.425 --> 25:11.927
- [Ha-kyung] Turn signal.
- [Ki-jun] Oh.

25:12.802 --> 25:14.930
[engine rumbling]

25:17.265 --> 25:18.266
[chuckles]

25:19.142 --> 25:21.519
Some things don't ever change, right?

25:21.603 --> 25:22.771
I don't know.

25:26.024 --> 25:27.150
[sighs]

25:27.692 --> 25:30.237
Ha-kyung, what am I gonna do?

25:31.738 --> 25:34.532
- Leave her if you have to.
- What? How can you even say that?

25:36.159 --> 25:37.369
I can't do that.

25:37.452 --> 25:39.204
I love her way too much to do that to her.

25:40.247 --> 25:41.248
Then just let it go.

25:41.831 --> 25:44.417
It's that guy, Lee Si-woo did this.

25:44.501 --> 25:46.878
What? No, it's not.
It's just between you and her.

25:47.504 --> 25:50.006
You're so defensive when Lee Si-woo
comes up. What's with you?

25:51.216 --> 25:53.468
It's not him. It's about you
blaming things on him.

25:53.551 --> 25:55.845
- [playful music]
- [inhales]

25:56.846 --> 25:58.515
- [scoffs]
- [Ki-jun sighs]

25:58.598 --> 26:00.267
Be careful, Jin Ha-kyung.

26:00.892 --> 26:04.396
I can tell, he goes to women
like they're nothing.

26:05.522 --> 26:06.439
[scoffs]

26:07.607 --> 26:10.068
Keep your eyes on the road.
You should focus.

26:11.027 --> 26:13.738
I'm just looking out for you,
like a big brother would've.

26:13.822 --> 26:18.493
Kick Senior Um and that guy,
out of the apartment today. Okay?

26:18.576 --> 26:20.537
[scoffs]
Big brother, my ass.

26:21.204 --> 26:24.249
So stay out. And it's not your business.
I'm handling it.

26:25.667 --> 26:27.961
[playful music continues]

26:31.381 --> 26:33.008
[exhales sharply]

26:37.095 --> 26:38.430
[music stops]

26:40.390 --> 26:41.391
[sighs]

26:43.101 --> 26:43.935
[smacks lips]

26:45.145 --> 26:46.146
[mouse clicks]

26:46.229 --> 26:48.690
[door opens]

26:50.150 --> 26:52.319
- [door closes]
- It's so hot.

26:52.402 --> 26:53.486
[groans]

26:54.279 --> 26:56.740
[sighs]
I heard the computer room

26:56.823 --> 26:59.701
is nice and cold,
because the computer's got new AC.

26:59.784 --> 27:01.202
So how can it be so hot in here?

27:01.286 --> 27:03.663
The computers won't work
if they get too hot.

27:03.747 --> 27:06.791
And they think we can?
They like the machines better than us.

27:07.500 --> 27:10.128
It's so unfair.
With the hours we're putting in?

27:10.211 --> 27:11.796
I'm sure we work just as hard.

27:11.880 --> 27:13.590
[chuckles]
That's true.

27:15.050 --> 27:16.301
[Eun-ji clicks tongue, sighs]

27:16.384 --> 27:17.719
[cell phone buzzing]

27:18.803 --> 27:20.096
Yes, this is Yu-jin.

27:24.976 --> 27:26.561
[hurried footsteps receding]

27:29.898 --> 27:33.818
What do you mean the feature article
seems like it'll fall through?

27:33.902 --> 27:36.654
Your husband just called
earlier this morning,

27:36.738 --> 27:38.740
and we discussed things.

27:38.823 --> 27:41.242
According to him,
there's too much on his plate.

27:41.326 --> 27:43.703
Why didn't he turn it down earlier?

27:43.787 --> 27:46.873
The society section's been finalized!
I don't have time for this!

27:46.956 --> 27:49.459
Oh. I'm so sorry.

27:50.377 --> 27:51.336
Uh…

27:52.212 --> 27:54.631
Let me… I'll go talk to him now.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.008
Let me get back to you.

27:57.092 --> 27:58.426
Yes, I'm sorry, sir.

27:59.552 --> 28:00.595
Okay.

28:03.390 --> 28:04.432
[sighs]

28:04.516 --> 28:06.518
[somber music]

28:08.853 --> 28:09.771
[sighs]

28:11.523 --> 28:14.275
Do you know how many computers
are running in here?

28:14.359 --> 28:17.487
And we can't open the windows.
It's like we're being steamed.

28:17.570 --> 28:20.657
Computer room got a new AC,
and it's really cold.

28:20.740 --> 28:22.534
Can't we have that too?

28:23.284 --> 28:24.160
When?

28:25.370 --> 28:26.287
[sighs]

28:27.038 --> 28:29.416
Okay. Please hurry if you can.

28:31.918 --> 28:33.086
Well?

28:33.169 --> 28:35.130
They're here, but we'll have to wait.

28:35.213 --> 28:37.257
They said it'll take a few hours.

28:37.340 --> 28:38.967
- [Myung-ju] Again?
- [sighs]

28:39.050 --> 28:41.177
That's what they said an hour ago.

28:41.261 --> 28:42.303
Mm.

28:44.723 --> 28:46.099
Mr. Shin, can you try to negotiate?

28:47.183 --> 28:48.226
[inhales]
Why?

28:48.309 --> 28:50.103
'Cause you're really good at it.

28:53.982 --> 28:54.941
[sighs]

28:55.900 --> 28:57.318
Hey, Lee Si…

29:01.281 --> 29:03.575
Mr. Lee's a little out of it today.

29:03.658 --> 29:04.576
[sighs]

29:04.659 --> 29:07.120
I bet he feels
like he's getting steamed too.

29:09.247 --> 29:10.206
Well, Mr. Shin?

29:10.874 --> 29:12.167
I can go.

29:12.250 --> 29:14.043
No, no.

29:14.127 --> 29:15.670
I'm going.

29:15.754 --> 29:17.380
I'll check it. Okay.

29:19.174 --> 29:20.049
Thank you.

29:20.133 --> 29:21.342
[Soo-jin sighs]

29:24.095 --> 29:26.097
AIR CONDITIONING ROOM
RESTRICTED ACCESS

29:26.181 --> 29:27.265
[sighs]

29:28.224 --> 29:29.642
[thumping]

29:30.685 --> 29:32.979
Hello, I'm from the Chief Team.

29:33.062 --> 29:34.481
[exhales]

29:36.232 --> 29:38.234
Doesn't even sound like they're working.

29:39.736 --> 29:40.612
[sighs]

29:42.113 --> 29:44.073
When will the air conditioner…

29:45.450 --> 29:46.785
[blows air]

29:46.868 --> 29:49.162
[steam hissing]

29:50.330 --> 29:51.164
[exhales deeply]

29:52.332 --> 29:53.666
Is there something you want?

29:54.375 --> 29:55.335
[sighs]

29:56.294 --> 29:57.670
Ah, yeah.

29:58.630 --> 30:00.715
Thank you for everything. Thanks.

30:01.674 --> 30:03.927
[melancholy music]

30:04.010 --> 30:05.386
[deep inhale]

30:06.888 --> 30:07.847
[exhales deeply]

30:12.477 --> 30:13.686
[Tae-kyung] Four toes.

30:14.312 --> 30:15.438
Four.

30:16.606 --> 30:18.817
- One, two, three, four.
- [cheeky music]

30:18.900 --> 30:21.611
On their hind legs,
alligators have four toes.

30:23.196 --> 30:24.280
[exhales deeply]

30:24.989 --> 30:27.158
[cheeky music continues]

30:29.202 --> 30:30.411
- [door opens]
- [gasps]

30:30.495 --> 30:31.621
Hey.

30:32.622 --> 30:35.792
The details are almost worked out
for Ha-kyung's blind date.

30:35.875 --> 30:37.752
They'll send a few dates that work,

30:37.836 --> 30:40.296
and then we get to pick
the final date for the date.

30:40.380 --> 30:42.590
[sighs]
Ma, you haven't given up yet?

30:42.674 --> 30:44.467
He's a gynecologist.

30:44.551 --> 30:48.304
So he's got an excellent future
and more than enough money, you know?

30:48.888 --> 30:50.765
[sighs]
Let it go.

30:50.849 --> 30:53.810
It's nearly monsoon season,
I'm sure she's got enough to think about.

30:53.893 --> 30:56.646
If you keep setting things up
without asking,

30:56.729 --> 30:58.439
she will cut you off.

30:58.523 --> 30:59.399
[sighs]

31:00.149 --> 31:04.904
What are you gonna do in life,
when I have another accident and I die?

31:04.988 --> 31:08.116
You and Ha-kyung are hopeless.
You can't do anything.

31:08.199 --> 31:12.328
'Cause when I leave this world,
I wanna know that you both have someone.

31:12.412 --> 31:14.414
Hopefully, they'll handle
planning my funeral.

31:14.497 --> 31:15.415
- Mother!
- [pen taps]

31:15.498 --> 31:16.749
You're fine! Don't say that!

31:16.833 --> 31:21.170
You think your mother will live forever
just to wait on you hand and foot?

31:21.254 --> 31:22.630
That's not what I said.

31:22.714 --> 31:25.550
Shut your mouth,
and you can help me or you can hush, okay?

31:25.633 --> 31:26.885
I'll do what I want!

31:26.968 --> 31:29.596
I try to keep you two from fighting,
but I'll knock it off!

31:30.430 --> 31:33.516
You don't know how lucky you are
to have a mom like me.

31:34.601 --> 31:35.435
[slams]

31:37.103 --> 31:38.396
[exhales deeply]

31:39.272 --> 31:41.941
Why can't she ever let me
get my work done?

31:43.067 --> 31:46.863
Oh, shit. Where was my train
of thought? Shit!

31:46.946 --> 31:49.240
[engine revving]

31:55.038 --> 31:56.372
[engine stops]

32:08.301 --> 32:10.637
[dramatic music]

32:12.639 --> 32:15.350
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

32:16.559 --> 32:17.477
[sighs]

32:25.777 --> 32:27.820
Oh, Mr. Lee, you came down?

32:30.573 --> 32:31.824
I have to talk to you.

32:33.368 --> 32:34.285
Okay.

32:37.372 --> 32:38.331
Hm?

32:38.414 --> 32:41.417
[cell phone buzzing]

32:42.752 --> 32:44.420
HONEY

32:46.297 --> 32:47.256
[sighs]

32:47.882 --> 32:49.926
[pensive music]

32:52.387 --> 32:53.763
KI-JUN

32:57.308 --> 33:00.520
- [line ringing]
- [sighs]

33:06.150 --> 33:09.612
[cell phone buzzing]

33:12.573 --> 33:14.075
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON

33:15.702 --> 33:16.786
[door closes]

33:16.869 --> 33:18.955
[dramatic music continues]

33:26.671 --> 33:28.381
What's wrong? Are you okay?

33:30.508 --> 33:32.051
I heard there was a car accident.

33:32.969 --> 33:33.970
Are you all right?

33:35.805 --> 33:38.349
Of course. It was a minor accident.
And they towed my car.

33:39.517 --> 33:41.519
Han Ki-jun's suspicious. This was risky.

33:41.602 --> 33:42.770
Maybe I want him to find out.

33:43.521 --> 33:44.355
Huh?

33:44.439 --> 33:46.107
Why did you call Mr. Um?

33:46.190 --> 33:48.317
Why couldn't you text me that you're okay?

33:48.901 --> 33:50.403
I called, so he'd cover me.

33:50.486 --> 33:53.781
Why did Han Ki-jun go
to pick you up, then?

33:55.158 --> 33:56.868
Well, I needed him for my insurance.

33:56.951 --> 33:59.412
How many reasons are there
for Han Ki-jun to see you?

34:00.204 --> 34:01.289
It seems endless.

34:01.372 --> 34:02.790
When is it over?

34:02.874 --> 34:05.334
The column, the apology,
and now car insurance?

34:06.335 --> 34:08.337
I need to know what else is left.

34:08.421 --> 34:11.007
[somber music]

34:12.050 --> 34:13.843
What's been happening with you?

34:13.926 --> 34:16.179
I'm sick and tired of Han Ki-jun.
It's pissing me off!

34:18.306 --> 34:21.893
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

34:23.644 --> 34:26.230
I heard about the accident,
and you weren't responding to me.

34:26.981 --> 34:28.608
[inhales]
If you were hurt,

34:28.691 --> 34:30.735
there was no one I could ask,
how would I know?

34:31.319 --> 34:33.362
I've been worried sick all morning.

34:33.946 --> 34:37.450
The whole meeting, I, I couldn't
do anything but worry about you.

34:39.243 --> 34:41.287
It was impossible
to think of anything else.

34:41.788 --> 34:44.123
[dramatic music continues]

34:45.458 --> 34:46.667
[Si-woo] In an instant,

34:47.335 --> 34:49.378
it felt like my feelings for you tripled.

34:50.922 --> 34:54.175
But the more they grow,
so do the problems.

34:55.009 --> 34:57.053
And I grow angrier too.

35:00.389 --> 35:03.601
It was nothing but a fender bender,
and everyone was just fine.

35:03.684 --> 35:05.853
I didn't realize
it would worry you like this.

35:09.023 --> 35:10.149
I'm sorry.

35:11.400 --> 35:12.443
[sighs]

35:13.152 --> 35:15.196
You have to stop apologizing.

35:15.279 --> 35:17.115
It makes me feel like I'm the bad guy.

35:17.698 --> 35:19.367
'Cause you really didn't do
anything wrong.

35:21.994 --> 35:24.205
[somber music]

35:27.083 --> 35:28.501
[cell phone buzzes]

35:30.378 --> 35:32.839
[somber music continues]

35:35.424 --> 35:37.426
They scheduled a briefing for later today.

35:39.262 --> 35:40.471
You should get ready.

35:47.436 --> 35:49.605
[somber music]

35:52.984 --> 35:53.985
[music stops]

35:55.528 --> 35:56.571
[sighs]

35:56.654 --> 35:58.656
[somber music]

36:00.867 --> 36:03.119
[birds twittering]

36:08.374 --> 36:09.625
Si-woo.

36:14.964 --> 36:16.132
Can we talk?

36:19.635 --> 36:22.221
- It makes sense. Here.
- Mm.

36:24.390 --> 36:26.767
- [Ha-kyung] So sorry I'm late, everyone.
- Oh, it's fine.

36:26.851 --> 36:28.436
[inhales]
Is everything okay with your car?

36:28.519 --> 36:30.313
And you're, you're okay, right?

36:32.190 --> 36:34.650
- The car needs work, but I'm okay.
- Oh.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.485
I hear there's gonna be
a briefing this afternoon?

36:36.569 --> 36:37.445
Oh.

36:37.528 --> 36:39.697
Can I see the minutes
from the call this morning?

36:39.780 --> 36:41.073
Yeah, of course.

36:41.949 --> 36:45.328
There wasn't anything too out of line
from what we said at the last one.

36:45.870 --> 36:49.749
By Okinawa, there's a stationary front
formed over the sea.

36:49.832 --> 36:52.043
Due to the trough
from northern central China,

36:52.126 --> 36:54.629
combined with the formation of a gale,

36:54.712 --> 36:57.256
it's looking like monsoon season
starts in five days,

36:57.340 --> 36:59.759
and it'll start with Jeju
and parts of the south.

37:01.010 --> 37:02.637
It's just not sitting right with me.

37:03.638 --> 37:04.555
You think it's wrong?

37:04.639 --> 37:07.975
Over the Okhotsk Sea,
there's an abnormal anticyclone.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.269
Plus, we got cold air
coming down from the north.

37:10.353 --> 37:13.314
If the anticyclone
from the North Pacific weakens,

37:13.981 --> 37:17.777
it'll delay the stationary front
and take longer for it to rise up north.

37:19.528 --> 37:21.155
And what does the data say?

37:21.239 --> 37:22.698
It's almost the same as yesterday.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.450
What do we do?

37:25.326 --> 37:27.119
Your thoughts, Forecaster?

37:34.627 --> 37:37.672
For the briefing, we'll stick
to what was discussed this morning.

37:37.755 --> 37:40.549
I'm not saying I disagree,
it's just if we're changing that much,

37:40.633 --> 37:42.134
we need proof.

37:42.218 --> 37:44.303
Of course. Let's do that.

37:44.387 --> 37:46.013
- Miss Kim.
- Yes, Director?

37:46.097 --> 37:49.141
I need some data on anticipated changes
to that Chinese trough.

37:49.225 --> 37:51.269
- Please send it to the briefing room.
- Yes, ma'am.

37:54.355 --> 37:55.982
[footsteps receding]

38:00.027 --> 38:00.945
[mumbles]

38:03.322 --> 38:05.574
What happened with you
and my husband last night?

38:05.658 --> 38:08.703
He found me. He showed up at the door.

38:09.412 --> 38:10.830
My husband came to your house?

38:10.913 --> 38:12.164
To Director Jin's house.

38:12.873 --> 38:14.542
He was already drunk too.

38:14.625 --> 38:17.378
What? Why did he go to her?

38:21.299 --> 38:22.341
[exhales]

38:23.551 --> 38:24.969
Tell me!

38:26.012 --> 38:27.430
I think Ki-jun found out.

38:27.513 --> 38:28.806
What?

38:28.889 --> 38:31.267
That you and I lived together.

38:31.350 --> 38:33.394
[dramatic music]

38:34.270 --> 38:35.438
Who said so?

38:35.521 --> 38:36.981
You didn't tell him, did you?

38:38.149 --> 38:39.317
You think I would?

38:39.400 --> 38:40.860
I have no reason to.

38:42.028 --> 38:43.237
[sighs]

38:44.196 --> 38:45.197
Oh!

38:45.990 --> 38:48.159
I knew something was wrong.
He's been so weird.

38:48.242 --> 38:49.785
Oh! Oh, no.

38:50.453 --> 38:53.164
It's gonna be fine.
You didn't do anything wrong.

38:53.247 --> 38:55.875
Just tell him it was all
before you knew him.

38:56.542 --> 38:57.752
It's not that simple.

38:58.502 --> 39:00.921
He's not the kind of guy
who'd just let it go.

39:01.005 --> 39:03.966
I know exactly how he was gonna react,
even though it's in the past.

39:04.050 --> 39:06.052
Oh, it sucks!

39:07.678 --> 39:10.931
We moved in together,
because we loved each other so much.

39:11.724 --> 39:15.895
You said you would never regret
acting out of love. You said that.

39:15.978 --> 39:18.814
Well, love changes,
and my feelings about it changed too.

39:19.732 --> 39:22.485
Back then, I was sure. I knew.
But now it's different.

39:23.110 --> 39:24.737
I'd give anything to change it.

39:25.237 --> 39:26.447
Like you wouldn't?

39:27.031 --> 39:28.157
No.

39:28.240 --> 39:29.617
I don't regret it at all.

39:29.700 --> 39:32.078
'Cause I know I was doing what I could.

39:32.161 --> 39:34.914
[sighs]
Sure, you'll think that for now.

39:34.997 --> 39:37.333
When you get a girlfriend,
you'll change your mind.

39:37.416 --> 39:39.960
You'll hate that you used to live with me
at one time then.

39:40.044 --> 39:42.129
[dramatic music continues]

39:43.631 --> 39:44.548
[sighs]

39:47.176 --> 39:48.928
Well, I told her.

39:52.473 --> 39:55.601
Wait, you're dating someone, like now?

39:55.684 --> 39:56.936
Yeah.

39:57.520 --> 39:59.230
And I think you should tell him the truth.

39:59.730 --> 40:01.565
When you really love someone,

40:01.649 --> 40:03.984
you love everything,
even things from the past.

40:04.068 --> 40:05.736
He'll move on and accept it.

40:06.237 --> 40:08.906
[dramatic music]

40:16.539 --> 40:18.499
[footsteps receding]

40:21.627 --> 40:23.504
[Myung-ju sighs]
So hot.

40:25.423 --> 40:26.674
Lee Si-woo.

40:27.341 --> 40:29.260
- Yeah?
- Where did you go?

40:30.719 --> 40:31.971
[Dong-han] Something wrong?

40:32.054 --> 40:33.889
You were spacey this morning too.

40:33.973 --> 40:35.808
Seriously, your head's been in the sky.

40:36.392 --> 40:37.685
I'm sorry, sir.

40:37.768 --> 40:39.979
[Myung-ju] It's the heat.
It's throwing all of us off.

40:40.062 --> 40:41.730
No one's focused with the heat, you know?

40:44.942 --> 40:46.318
Oh, Miss Kim, can I see that?

40:47.611 --> 40:49.989
This is the data predicting
the trough's course.

40:50.072 --> 40:52.366
You can deliver this to the briefing room.

40:52.450 --> 40:54.743
And I know it's hot, still,
you've gotta step up.

40:57.121 --> 40:57.997
Sure.

41:00.916 --> 41:01.917
[inhales]

41:04.753 --> 41:05.838
He could be sick.

41:11.677 --> 41:13.679
[sighs]
It is hot in here.

41:13.762 --> 41:15.055
[sniffles]

41:16.056 --> 41:17.016
[groans]

41:29.737 --> 41:31.322
Is it anyone I've met?

41:33.532 --> 41:34.992
The girl you've been seeing.

41:35.075 --> 41:37.870
She's not anyone that works here, is she?

41:39.371 --> 41:40.414
[document rustles]

41:43.209 --> 41:44.084
[sighs]

41:45.669 --> 41:48.255
That's all we can say, currently,
about the start of monsoon season,

41:48.339 --> 41:51.258
I'll pass things to Director Jin Ha-kyung
from Chief Team

41:51.342 --> 41:53.010
to elaborate further and answer questions.

41:55.304 --> 41:56.430
[thuds]

41:59.600 --> 42:01.435
I'm Director Jin from Chief Team Two.

42:01.519 --> 42:02.978
Let's start with questions.

42:06.148 --> 42:08.025
I'm from JBC, Reporter Cho Eun-ji.

42:08.108 --> 42:10.069
Your reports claim
that the seasonal rain front

42:10.152 --> 42:12.446
should last longer than average this year.

42:12.530 --> 42:13.614
Why do you think so?

42:13.697 --> 42:16.408
It has to do with the influence
of the North Pacific's anticyclone.

42:16.492 --> 42:18.953
We think it will reach China
and stay there.

42:19.036 --> 42:21.247
What day do you think
the monsoons will end? Do you know?

42:21.330 --> 42:22.498
Well, we won't state a date.

42:22.581 --> 42:24.583
Probably two or three days later
than average.

42:24.667 --> 42:26.585
Also, I'd like to clarify
some of the terminology.

42:26.669 --> 42:27.503
[door opens]

42:33.217 --> 42:35.636
- [tense music]
- [door closes]

42:41.600 --> 42:43.936
A significant reason
we're hesitant to give

42:44.019 --> 42:45.604
a predicted end date

42:45.688 --> 42:49.400
is because the weather during the summer
is breaking pattern due to climate change.

42:49.483 --> 42:51.569
[Ha-kyung] In the interest
of avoiding false promises

42:51.652 --> 42:53.654
with start and end dates for the rain,

42:53.737 --> 42:57.116
we've decided that short-range
and weekly forecasts are more appropriate.

42:57.199 --> 42:59.285
[tense music continues]

43:01.203 --> 43:02.121
For you.

43:05.624 --> 43:07.209
Moving on to the next question.

43:09.628 --> 43:12.715
You walked in with Yu-jin.
Why did that happen?

43:12.798 --> 43:15.467
Well, I don't know.

43:17.386 --> 43:19.638
You don't know? That doesn't make sense.

43:19.722 --> 43:22.766
My history with her is in the past,
so I don't care and I don't know.

43:22.850 --> 43:23.767
Come again?

43:24.518 --> 43:26.270
I understand how to let the past go.

43:26.353 --> 43:30.524
If I found out something I didn't know,
I'd never harass my ex at her house.

43:30.608 --> 43:32.651
You know, that'll make me
seem like a loser.

43:32.735 --> 43:34.778
[tense music]

43:37.823 --> 43:39.366
[sighs]

43:43.203 --> 43:45.414
[keyboards clacking]

43:49.668 --> 43:52.504
[dramatic music]

43:52.588 --> 43:55.591
[woman 1] I heard she was living
with a KMA employee.

43:55.674 --> 43:58.969
I guess she ended up marrying that guy.

43:59.053 --> 44:03.307
[woman 2] Married after living together?
Lived together… Lived together.

44:03.390 --> 44:06.143
Lived together… Lived together…

44:06.935 --> 44:09.605
Lived together… Lived together…

44:13.150 --> 44:15.152
[tense music]

44:29.333 --> 44:31.502
[tense music continues]

44:51.772 --> 44:53.315
[clattering]

44:55.609 --> 44:57.945
[tense music rises]

45:05.202 --> 45:06.203
This is all your fault!

45:06.286 --> 45:07.663
[Ki-jun] And you know it!

45:07.746 --> 45:10.249
[crowd clamoring]

45:11.041 --> 45:12.668
Come on, be honest with yourself.

45:12.751 --> 45:15.170
You think you're such a gentleman
while she's in agony?

45:15.254 --> 45:16.672
Just grow up and be a man.

45:16.755 --> 45:17.798
Well, I will.

45:17.881 --> 45:19.049
[groans]

45:19.675 --> 45:20.509
Hey.
[gasps]

45:21.885 --> 45:24.596
[crowd clamoring]

45:26.348 --> 45:27.641
Lee Si-woo, quit it!

45:27.724 --> 45:29.268
Stop them!

45:31.687 --> 45:33.021
[grunts]

45:33.772 --> 45:35.399
[overlapping chatter]

45:35.482 --> 45:37.025
Wanna ruin my life, you bastard?

45:37.109 --> 45:38.610
You've really been pissing me off!

45:38.694 --> 45:39.820
[grunting]

45:40.904 --> 45:41.780
[man 1] Call somebody.

45:41.864 --> 45:43.157
- Hey!
- Let go of me!

45:43.240 --> 45:45.742
- [men clamoring]
- [Ki-jun] Let go!

45:47.578 --> 45:49.329
You have no idea who you're dealing with.

45:49.413 --> 45:51.331
- Let go! Please…
- [man 2] Stop!

45:51.415 --> 45:52.499
[grunts]
Come on!

45:52.583 --> 45:55.377
[grumbling]

45:55.461 --> 45:57.129
FORECAST BUREAU DIRECTOR GENERAL
KO BONG-CHAN

45:57.880 --> 45:59.381
Well done, both of you.

46:02.384 --> 46:04.428
[thumping]

46:06.263 --> 46:07.639
Hm? Great work.

46:11.059 --> 46:12.895
Never did I think we'd sink this low.

46:14.104 --> 46:17.566
I thought weather nerds didn't do
this kind of thing, you proved me wrong.

46:17.649 --> 46:19.735
[Bong-chan] So, tell me what happened.

46:19.818 --> 46:23.155
What, you two just wanted a fight
in front of the reporters for fun?

46:28.118 --> 46:29.119
Really? Nothing?

46:32.706 --> 46:33.749
Well, okay.

46:34.708 --> 46:35.584
Hey, Mr. Park.

46:36.168 --> 46:37.044
Yes?

46:37.127 --> 46:41.006
I want written apologies from those two,
and whatever else HR says.

46:41.507 --> 46:42.549
Yes, sir.

46:45.552 --> 46:46.553
[door opens]

46:47.513 --> 46:49.389
On today, of all days.

46:52.184 --> 46:54.186
[playful music]

46:58.607 --> 47:00.692
[keyboard clacking]

47:02.778 --> 47:03.612
[Ha-kyung sighs]

47:04.780 --> 47:06.532
What do you think made them fight?

47:06.615 --> 47:09.701
It's so hot outside. We have no AC inside.

47:09.785 --> 47:12.579
No, they wouldn't fight,
just 'cause they're too warm.

47:13.747 --> 47:15.415
Not in front of that many people.

47:16.750 --> 47:17.668
[exhales]

47:19.628 --> 47:21.129
I have tea.

47:22.047 --> 47:23.590
You know Mr. Han's wife, right?

47:23.674 --> 47:24.675
The reporter?

47:24.758 --> 47:28.011
Well, can you guess
who in the building is her ex-boyfriend?

47:30.097 --> 47:31.098
You're kidding.

47:31.181 --> 47:32.224
It's true.

47:32.307 --> 47:35.018
- But it's true. Lee Si-woo dated her.
- Whoa!

47:35.102 --> 47:37.104
[quirky music]

47:39.648 --> 47:40.732
[whispers]
Seriously?

47:41.608 --> 47:43.110
Wait, hang on.

47:43.819 --> 47:47.364
Then her husband and her ex have been
working together every day,

47:47.447 --> 47:49.700
and they couldn't take it
and fought over her?

47:50.284 --> 47:52.578
But why? She already married Mr. Han.

47:53.161 --> 47:54.997
Maybe she cheated on him with Lee Si-woo.

47:56.206 --> 47:57.874
- [gasps]
- [Seok-ho] I don't think so.

47:57.958 --> 48:00.794
Si-woo's too willing to stick
to his guns and that.

48:01.753 --> 48:04.756
There's no way he'd go back
to a relationship that ended a while ago.

48:05.591 --> 48:08.635
I think there's something else
bothering him.

48:08.719 --> 48:10.220
[gasps]
Okay, but what would that be?

48:10.304 --> 48:11.513
Okay, what do you know?

48:12.097 --> 48:13.223
[Ha-kyung] If I had to guess…

48:14.224 --> 48:16.476
If someone was baiting the other,
it was Han Ki-jun.

48:17.519 --> 48:19.646
I'd know. After ten years, I can say.

48:20.647 --> 48:21.773
He's irrational.

48:23.191 --> 48:24.359
Mm.

48:25.110 --> 48:28.405
So I think it'd be best
if all of us didn't bring it up again.

48:28.488 --> 48:31.825
Lee Si-woo's struggling today.
And I expect you all to respect that.

48:33.660 --> 48:34.620
Of course.

48:34.703 --> 48:37.789
Dissecting the love lives
of our co-workers isn't worth our time.

48:37.873 --> 48:41.585
And so, huh,
it won't come up again, director.

48:42.336 --> 48:43.170
It's over.

48:49.217 --> 48:50.218
Yeah. Whatever.

48:50.969 --> 48:52.804
- Hm.
- Hm.

48:58.018 --> 48:59.019
[sighs]

49:00.354 --> 49:02.564
[AC humming]

49:05.025 --> 49:06.818
Oh, the AC's on.

49:06.902 --> 49:07.778
[Myung-ju] Oh!

49:07.861 --> 49:09.905
[light music]

49:09.988 --> 49:11.740
Hey, so whatever you said to them worked.

49:11.823 --> 49:12.866
[scoffs]

49:12.949 --> 49:15.702
I just didn't do anything, really.

49:17.996 --> 49:18.997
[sighs]

49:19.081 --> 49:20.707
[Seok-ho] Thanks for your help.

49:21.458 --> 49:22.668
Especially in this heat.

49:22.751 --> 49:24.127
- Oh, thank you.
- Here.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.504
Thank you.

49:25.587 --> 49:27.047
Great.
[worker 1 chuckles]

49:28.340 --> 49:30.425
Please take one. Yeah.

49:30.509 --> 49:31.760
[worker 2] Oh, thank you.

49:32.386 --> 49:33.303
Oh, gosh.

49:34.054 --> 49:35.472
- That'll do.
- [exhales]

49:35.555 --> 49:37.641
- [worker 3] Wow, that's nice.
- [worker 4] Yeah.

49:38.600 --> 49:40.686
[light music continues]

49:46.566 --> 49:47.526
[exhales deeply]

49:48.402 --> 49:50.278
Oh, this is…

49:50.362 --> 49:52.072
UPCOMING RAINY SEASON
WILL BE HOT AND WORSE

49:52.155 --> 49:53.949
LOCAL GOVERNMENTS PREPARE
FOR THE RAINY SEASON

49:59.079 --> 49:59.913
[clicks tongue]

50:24.229 --> 50:26.189
[footsteps receding]

50:31.862 --> 50:34.573
[quirky music]

50:39.703 --> 50:40.954
Why her?

50:41.455 --> 50:42.664
[music fades]

50:46.168 --> 50:48.378
We wrapped up, so I'm heading out.

50:48.462 --> 50:49.671
Miss Lee.

50:49.755 --> 50:50.839
Take this.

50:51.465 --> 50:52.382
Oh.

50:53.133 --> 50:55.719
We can just do the usual transfer,
it's fine.

50:55.802 --> 50:58.346
I've already sent payment for this month.

50:58.430 --> 51:00.223
Think of this like a tip.

51:01.016 --> 51:03.226
Oh, you're too kind.

51:03.310 --> 51:04.895
[crickets chirping]

51:04.978 --> 51:08.565
By the way, has something been
happening at home recently?

51:09.399 --> 51:11.318
Uh, no. Why?

51:11.401 --> 51:16.198
My kid said that teacher was distracted
in the lessons lately, so…

51:17.491 --> 51:18.492
Oh.

51:18.575 --> 51:21.203
You know, kids pick up
on more than we think.

51:21.286 --> 51:23.163
So I hope everything's okay.

51:24.206 --> 51:26.374
Yeah. I apologize, ma'am.

51:27.501 --> 51:28.877
See you next week.

51:28.960 --> 51:30.712
Okay. Get home safe.

51:30.796 --> 51:33.048
[crickets chirping]

51:35.467 --> 51:36.676
[clatters, squeaks]

51:43.016 --> 51:44.893
[crickets chirping]

51:52.984 --> 51:54.986
[somber music]

52:10.502 --> 52:12.629
[somber music continues]

52:15.549 --> 52:19.386
CALLS

52:19.469 --> 52:22.222
BO-MI'S DAD

52:27.310 --> 52:29.771
[somber music]

52:33.692 --> 52:36.111
KMA ANNOUNCES
THIS YEAR'S RAINY SEASON PROSPECT

52:36.987 --> 52:38.029
[doorbell chimes]

52:39.239 --> 52:40.615
[clinking]

52:42.784 --> 52:45.537
[somber music continues]

52:47.747 --> 52:48.832
[cell phone buzzes]

52:48.915 --> 52:50.500
WIFE

52:53.962 --> 52:56.298
- Hey, how are you?
- [Hyang-rae] Where are you?

52:57.757 --> 52:59.718
At the KMA, like always.

52:59.801 --> 53:00.927
Where in the building?

53:02.053 --> 53:03.305
Night-duty room.

53:04.180 --> 53:05.348
Is it comfortable enough?

53:06.182 --> 53:07.100
Well…

53:07.684 --> 53:10.061
I hardly think about it. We're so busy.

53:10.729 --> 53:13.940
Today was chaotic, we've out of break,
'cause we announced the rainy season.

53:14.024 --> 53:15.525
It's my first break today.

53:16.484 --> 53:17.652
It must be hard.

53:18.528 --> 53:20.405
Uh, it's fine.
[chuckles]

53:21.740 --> 53:22.699
Ah.

53:24.868 --> 53:26.202
Okay, then. See you.

53:26.786 --> 53:28.538
- Oh, um, is Bo-mi doing…
- [line chimes]

53:35.712 --> 53:36.588
[inhales]

53:37.213 --> 53:38.298
[sighs]

53:48.433 --> 53:49.976
[pensive music]

53:50.060 --> 53:51.227
[guard] He said what?

53:51.311 --> 53:53.355
Mr. Um went home hours ago.

53:54.105 --> 53:55.398
Oh, yes.

53:55.482 --> 53:57.359
He's not here. He left a while ago.

53:57.442 --> 53:59.527
[pensive music continues]

53:59.611 --> 54:01.613
Well, then I better get home, huh.

54:01.696 --> 54:03.031
Thanks for everything.

54:03.865 --> 54:05.450
Of course. Good evening.

54:09.704 --> 54:11.706
[pensive music]

54:19.339 --> 54:21.591
[pensive music continues]

54:31.643 --> 54:32.769
Jeez.

54:32.852 --> 54:34.688
[indistinct chatter]

54:36.439 --> 54:40.860
[groaning]

54:40.944 --> 54:41.903
Come on!

54:44.698 --> 54:46.574
[indistinct chatter]

54:54.332 --> 54:55.250
Here.

54:56.543 --> 54:57.627
Ah!

54:57.711 --> 55:00.088
Aw, I didn't know you were so sensitive.

55:01.214 --> 55:03.133
So, are you upset?

55:03.675 --> 55:05.260
You don't approve if you're asking.

55:05.343 --> 55:08.096
He started it. What did you want me to do?
He starts punching.

55:08.179 --> 55:09.472
Do I just stand there?

55:09.556 --> 55:10.515
[sighs]

55:11.975 --> 55:13.184
Well, it's not his fault.

55:15.812 --> 55:18.106
The columns and the insurance
are my doing.

55:18.189 --> 55:20.400
And I know it's strange
that I still call him.

55:20.483 --> 55:23.778
Ten years together, it left us entangled
in unexpected ways.

55:24.362 --> 55:27.157
And there are certain things
I can't cut off quite so easily.

55:29.534 --> 55:31.453
What happened this morning was,

55:32.037 --> 55:34.080
that he changed my insurance
without telling me,

55:34.164 --> 55:35.915
so his friend would get the commission.

55:35.999 --> 55:37.959
And in the moment, I was so stressed.

55:38.043 --> 55:40.670
The man in the other car kept yelling
about my insurance.

55:43.006 --> 55:46.009
And I thought if I left out
all these little details for you,

55:46.634 --> 55:49.387
then you might not judge me,
that you wouldn't know

55:50.180 --> 55:52.223
that my last relationship was so awful.

55:52.849 --> 55:54.059
And I could forget.

55:55.060 --> 55:56.186
So then…

55:57.395 --> 55:58.646
Why are you telling me this now?

56:01.024 --> 56:03.234
Well, I'd rather be embarrassed
for a second

56:03.860 --> 56:05.653
than have you wonder

56:06.529 --> 56:08.948
if I'm tricking you,
I'd rather have trust.

56:09.032 --> 56:11.034
[romantic music]

56:13.912 --> 56:16.498
Starting now,
you're getting total honesty.

56:17.916 --> 56:22.921
I can't promise exactly when all
of the pieces of Han Ki-jun will be gone

56:23.004 --> 56:24.297
and in my past.

56:25.590 --> 56:28.635
All I can say is that in the future,
I will share everything with you.

56:29.594 --> 56:30.929
I'm an open book.

56:31.513 --> 56:32.430
So…

56:32.514 --> 56:34.849
[romantic music continues]

56:37.685 --> 56:38.561
[sighs]

56:39.354 --> 56:40.814
This is getting out of hand.

56:42.607 --> 56:43.942
What are you feeling?

56:46.236 --> 56:49.197
I like you more than anyone I've known.

56:50.615 --> 56:52.325
And that's a little scary.

56:52.408 --> 56:55.203
[romantic music]

56:57.372 --> 57:00.917
It's getting to the point where I want
everyone to catch us and find out.

57:02.252 --> 57:05.463
Well, it's gonna be an issue,
'cause we'd have to call it off.

57:07.423 --> 57:09.801
[romantic music continues]

57:13.263 --> 57:15.098
What the… What if they saw you?

57:15.682 --> 57:17.225
It's not work. We're fine.

57:17.308 --> 57:19.018
It's a small world. You'll never know.

57:20.687 --> 57:22.313
If you're worried about appearances,

57:22.397 --> 57:25.984
you shouldn't even look at me,
'cause they can see it in your eyes.

57:26.067 --> 57:27.193
Jin Ha-kyung.

57:28.403 --> 57:29.487
[chuckles]

57:29.571 --> 57:31.281
"Jin Ha…" So…

57:33.283 --> 57:34.242
You're crazy!

57:35.076 --> 57:36.703
[Ha-kyung giggling]

57:39.289 --> 57:41.374
[romantic music]

57:48.381 --> 57:50.008
[music fades]

57:53.303 --> 57:55.805
[both laughing]

58:00.143 --> 58:01.394
There's no way.

58:09.819 --> 58:11.112
[inhales]

58:17.285 --> 58:18.203
What's going on?

58:21.247 --> 58:22.624
You have something to tell me.

58:23.833 --> 58:24.876
Don't you?

58:28.505 --> 58:30.465
I'm tired. Later.

58:31.716 --> 58:33.426
We used to live together.

58:35.512 --> 58:38.348
We had an apartment. We dated a while ago.

58:38.932 --> 58:40.016
Is that so wrong?

58:40.642 --> 58:44.020
Well, that was before I knew you.
It's not that bad.

58:44.103 --> 58:45.980
There's nothing wrong
with living together.

58:47.482 --> 58:48.650
No, there's…

58:54.155 --> 58:55.114
[inhales]

58:57.492 --> 58:59.077
You're right. There isn't.

58:59.160 --> 59:02.163
It's not illegal.
I don't think it's even unethical.

59:02.247 --> 59:03.915
I know that.
[inhales]

59:03.998 --> 59:06.084
It's killing me still, Yu-jin.

59:07.919 --> 59:09.379
"I wish I never knew."

59:09.462 --> 59:12.090
"Just pretend you didn't hear.
Pretend you don't know."

59:13.550 --> 59:15.760
It's stuck and there's nothing I can do.

59:17.804 --> 59:20.515
I just can't deal with how you used to…

59:22.141 --> 59:24.143
live with someone else.
You get it, Yu-jin?

59:24.978 --> 59:27.897
And the fact that it was Lee Si-woo
kills me most of all.

59:29.148 --> 59:31.276
[sighs]
It was before I met you.

59:31.359 --> 59:32.902
Leave the past. Think about now.

59:32.986 --> 59:35.113
It's not over. If it were, maybe I could.

59:35.196 --> 59:37.490
What do you mean? I'm totally over him.

59:37.574 --> 59:38.825
Yu-jin, do you…

59:42.036 --> 59:43.079
Shit.

59:43.162 --> 59:44.372
[inhales]

59:45.748 --> 59:48.376
Do you know
who Lee Si-woo's dating right now?

59:50.044 --> 59:53.256
[Si-woo] Bad weather isn't always
as obvious as cloudy skies,

59:53.339 --> 59:57.719
unexpected snow and rain,
strong wind, and typhoons.

59:57.802 --> 59:59.387
It can be more subtle.

01:00:00.305 --> 01:00:02.265
So who's he dating?

01:00:02.807 --> 01:00:04.976
[dramatic music]

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:07.061
Jin Ha-kyung.

01:00:12.233 --> 01:00:13.318
Huh?

01:00:14.235 --> 01:00:15.111
Who's that?

01:00:15.194 --> 01:00:16.654
My ex-fiancée.

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:19.449
The woman I spent ten years with.

01:00:20.033 --> 01:00:21.784
Director Jin Ha-kyung from Team Two!

01:00:24.162 --> 01:00:25.455
[music fades]

01:00:27.540 --> 01:00:28.458
[gasps]

01:00:31.794 --> 01:00:34.047
[Si-woo] Just like that,
we've been transformed,

01:00:35.298 --> 01:00:37.925
irritable and unaware
that it's the weather's doing.

01:00:41.929 --> 01:00:44.015
[light music]

01:00:47.435 --> 01:00:48.603
[both chuckle]

01:00:49.771 --> 01:00:53.816
[Si-woo] If only it was as obvious
as a total downpour.

01:00:55.943 --> 01:00:57.945
[calm music]

01:01:06.829 --> 01:01:07.789
[sighs]

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:12.585
Well, that's not rain. Told ya.

01:01:12.669 --> 01:01:14.879
[calm music continues]

01:01:16.422 --> 01:01:19.509
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:26.349 --> 01:01:28.351
[closing theme music]

01:01:52.500 --> 01:01:54.544
- Are you dating Lee Si-woo?
- What?

01:01:54.627 --> 01:01:57.088
[Yu-jin] Aren't you just jealous,
because they're going out?

01:01:57.171 --> 01:01:59.006
Jealous? Of Si-woo?

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:00.717
[Si-woo] Why don't we just
let everyone know?

01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:02.009
[Ha-kyung] We have to play innocent.

01:02:03.219 --> 01:02:07.098
[Ki-jun] I'm sure that bastard Si-woo
approached Ha-kyung to get back at me.

01:02:08.224 --> 01:02:09.892
How is it coming along?
[laughs]

01:02:09.976 --> 01:02:12.520
Isn't making hasty conclusions
your specialty?

01:02:12.603 --> 01:02:14.689
Why don't you two have a debate about it?

01:02:15.857 --> 01:02:16.983
You should stop seeing her.

01:02:17.567 --> 01:02:19.736
[Ki-jun] Ha-kyung
doesn't date anyone sincerely

01:02:19.819 --> 01:02:21.529
unless they're a marriage prospect.
